@page "/video-editor"

@inject NavigationManager Nav
@using Ben.Web.Services

@*
    The old third host for the editor.

    This page mounted <VideoEditor> straight into page flow, with no height-constrained ancestor —
    the editor asks for height:100%, which against an auto-height <main> resolves to auto, so it
    sized itself to its content instead of to the window. It had no header, no project list and no
    link from anywhere on the site; the two pages people actually reach, My Videos and a case's
    Video tab, do the same job properly. Keeping a worse copy of a page alive costs a bug in three
    places every time the editor changes (2026-09-05 audit, site-9).

    It redirects rather than 404s because the address is in help, in bookmarks and in this repo's
    own test suite. The FeatureGate stays so a site with the editor switched off still says so
    instead of bouncing people to a page that will refuse them.
*@

<FeatureGate Flag="@SiteFeatures.VideoEditor">
    <PageTitle>Video Editor</PageTitle>
    <p class="text-muted">Taking you to My Videos…</p>
</FeatureGate>

@code {
    protected override void OnInitialized()
        => Nav.NavigateTo("/my-videos", replace: true);
}
